  <div class="fcx" aria-label="Axial Fans Manufacturers in Assam">
<section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-duo"><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-circle-question"></i></span><h2>What Are Axial Fans?</h2><p>Axial fans move air along the same axis as the rotating impeller. This operating principle makes them appropriate for applications where large quantities of air need to be moved effectively through a relatively direct airflow path.</p><p>There are two main types available in the Assam range: tube axial fans and vane axial fans. Tube axial fans are appropriate for long-distance duct airflow, while vane axial fans use guide vanes to improve static pressure and directional airflow control.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-rotate"></i></span><h2>How Axial Fans Work</h2><p>An axial fan draws air into the impeller and moves it forward along the axis of rotation. The rotating blades accelerate the air and create the required airflow through the fan casing and connected ventilation system.</p><p>Tube axial fans are especially useful where air needs to travel through ducts, tunnels, or commercial ventilation systems. Vane axial fans include aerodynamically shaped stationary guide vanes that help recover rotational swirl and convert it into useful static pressure.</p><p>The proper configuration depends on airflow volume, static pressure, duct arrangement, temperature, and the operating environment.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Types of Axial Fans</h2></div><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--2"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fan"></i></span><h3>Tube Axial Fans</h3><p>Tube Axial Fans Manufacturer solutions are designed for applications requiring high-volume airflow over longer distances. These fans feature a cylindrical casing and can be provided with aluminium alloy impellers with fixed or variable pitch blades.</p><p>The tube axial range is available in diameters from 315 mm to 1600 mm and may offer airflow up to 130,000 CFM. The casing is available in heavy-gauge hot-dip galvanized steel or SS304.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fan"></i></span><h3>Vane Axial Fans</h3><p>Vane Axial Fans Manufacturer solutions are designed with integrated downstream guide vanes. These guide vanes help recover swirl from the airflow and improve static pressure performance.</p><p>The available vane axial range offers overall efficiency of up to 88%. Motors are available with IP55/IP65 protection, Class H insulation, and fire-rated operation at 300°C for two hours. These fans are suitable for cooling towers, heat exchangers, and commercial HVAC plants.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Key Features of Axial Fans</h2><p>The main features of the axial fan range include:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>High-volume airflow performance</li><li>Tube axial and vane axial configurations</li><li>Aluminium alloy aerofoil impellers</li><li>Fixed and variable pitch options</li><li>Direct-driven and V-belt-driven configurations</li><li>Dynamically balanced impellers</li><li>ISO 1940 Grade G2.5 balancing</li><li>Hot-dip galvanized steel and SS304 casing options</li><li>High-temperature fire-rated configurations</li><li>Motor protection options including IP55 and IP65</li><li>Suitable for commercial and industrial ventilation</li></ul><p>The overall range covers impeller diameters from 315 mm to 1600 mm, with airflow from 1,000 to 180,000 CFM and static pressure up to 100 mm WG.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><div class="fcx-spec"><table class="fcx-table"><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Product</th><td>Axial Fans</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Impeller Diameter</th><td>315 mm to 1600 mm</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Overall Airflow</th><td>1,000 to 180,000 CFM</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Static Pressure</th><td>Up to 100 mm WG</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Temperature Rating</th><td>300°C / 400°C for 2 Hours Fire Rated</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Types</th><td>Tube Axial &amp; Vane Axial</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Impeller</th><td>Aluminium Alloy Aerofoil</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Blade Options</th><td>Fixed &amp; Variable Pitch</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Drive Options</th><td>Direct Drive / V-Belt Drive</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tube Axial Airflow</th><td>Up to 130,000 CFM</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tube Casing</th><td>Hot-Dip Galvanized Steel / SS304</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Vane Axial Efficiency</th><td>Up to 88% Total Efficiency</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Motor</th><td>IP55 / IP65, Class H</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="fcx-note"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-sliders"></i></span><div><p>These specifications are based on the current Assam Axial Fan product page. Final selection should be based on the actual airflow, static pressure, temperature, application, and site conditions.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Applications of Axial Fans</h2></div><p class="fcx-lead">Axial fans may be used in a wide range of commercial, industrial, and emergency ventilation systems.</p><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--3"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-industry"></i></span><h3>General Industrial Ventilation</h3><p>Factories and industrial facilities frequently require continuous air movement to remove hot, stale, or contaminated air. Axial fans can provide high-volume airflow for these ventilation requirements.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-temperature-half"></i></span><h3>Cooling Towers</h3><p>Vane axial fans may be used in cooling tower applications where large volumes of air need to be moved effectively through the system.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-temperature-half"></i></span><h3>Heat Exchangers</h3><p>Axial fans can support airflow around heat exchange equipment, helping circulate air through the specified cooling arrangement.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-industry"></i></span><h3>HVAC Plant Rooms</h3><p>Commercial and industrial HVAC plants can use axial fans for ventilation and air movement where high airflow is needed.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-road"></i></span><h3>Tunnels</h3><p>Tube axial fans are suitable for tunnel ventilation because they can move air through long passages and connected duct systems.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-temperature-half"></i></span><h3>Emergency Ventilation</h3><p>Fire-rated axial fan configurations may be used in applications where ventilation equipment needs to operate under high-temperature emergency conditions.</p><p>The Assam site identifies general and industrial ventilation, cooling towers, heat exchangers, HVAC plant rooms, and other large-air-volume applications.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Benefits of Axial Fans</h2><p>Properly selected axial fans can provide various practical advantages:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>High-volume airflow for large ventilation requirements</li><li>Efficient air movement along the fan axis</li><li>Suitable for long-distance duct applications</li><li>Multiple blade pitch options</li><li>Direct-drive and belt-drive configurations</li><li>Suitable for cooling and ventilation systems</li><li>Fire-rated options for emergency applications</li><li>Different casing materials for specific environments</li><li>Suitable for industrial and commercial projects</li><li>Compact airflow path compared with some other fan arrangements</li></ul><p>The actual performance depends on fan selection, system resistance, airflow requirements, installation conditions, and operating environment.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-blocks"><div class="fcx-block"><h2>Axial Fans Suppliers in Assam</h2><p><b>As Axial Fans Suppliers in Assam</b>, we provide tube axial and vane axial solutions for specific ventilation requirements. The fans may be selected according to airflow, static pressure, temperature, application, and site conditions.</p><p>Assam has a diverse industrial environment that includes tea processing units throughout the Brahmaputra Valley, refineries, oil and gas installations, cement plants, food-processing facilities, hospitals, and commercial buildings. The state's heavy monsoon and high humidity can make reliable ventilation and suitable corrosion-resistant construction vital considerations for certain projects.</p><p>For these applications, the appropriate fan configuration and casing material can be selected according to the actual project environment.</p></div><div class="fcx-block"><h2>Axial Fan Manufacturer in India</h2><p>The axial fans supplied for Assam projects are manufactured at the company's facility in Neemrana, Rajasthan. Each unit is selected according to the required airflow, static pressure, application, temperature, and location conditions.</p><p>Technical data and sizing support may be supplied before ordering. Finished equipment may be dispatched to project locations throughout Assam and other parts of India.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>How to Choose the Right Axial Fan</h2><p>Selecting the proper axial fan requires consideration of the complete ventilation system.</p><ul class="fcx-checks fcx-checks--long"><li><b>Airflow requirement:</b> Determine the specified CFM for the application.</li><li><b>Static pressure:</b> Calculate the pressure required to overcome duct and system resistance.</li><li><b>Fan type:</b> Select tube axial or vane axial according to the system design.</li><li><b>Fan diameter:</b> Choose the suitable impeller size according to the specified performance.</li><li><b>Blade pitch:</b> Consider fixed or variable pitch based on the operating requirement.</li><li><b>Drive arrangement:</b> Select direct drive or V-belt drive according to the application.</li><li><b>Temperature:</b> Check whether a standard or fire-rated configuration is needed.</li><li><b>Casing material:</b> Consider galvanized steel or SS304 according to the operating environment.</li><li><b>Site conditions:</b> Humidity, dust, temperature, installation area, and maintenance access should be considered.</li></ul><p>Providing proper airflow, pressure, temperature, and application details helps ensure the fan is properly matched to the ventilation system.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>FAQs</h2></div><div class="fcx-faq"><details><summary>What are axial fans used for?</summary><p>Axial fans are used for moving large volumes of air in industrial ventilation, cooling towers, heat exchangers, HVAC plant rooms, tunnels, and other ventilation applications.</p></details><details><summary>What sizes of axial fans are available?</summary><p>The available impeller diameter range is 315 mm to 1600 mm.</p></details><details><summary>What airflow capacity can these fans provide?</summary><p>The overall axial fan range offers airflow from 1,000 to 180,000 CFM, while the tube axial range offers airflow up to 130,000 CFM.</p></details><details><summary>What is the difference between tube axial and vane axial fans?</summary><p>Tube axial fans move air parallel to the fan axis and are suitable for applications such as ducts and tunnels. Vane axial fans use downstream guide vanes to improve static pressure and directional airflow control.</p></details><details><summary>Are fire-rated axial fans available?</summary><p>Yes. The listed range includes fire-rated configurations rated at 300°C / 400°C for 2 hours, depending on the chosen configuration.</p></details></div><div class="fcx-center" style="margin-top:26px"><a href="product.php" class="btn-cyber btn-cyber--primary fcx-btn" title="Fan Air India Products">Learn More <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-cta"><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Axial fans provide a practical solution for applications requiring high-volume air movement in commercial, industrial, HVAC, and emergency ventilation systems. With tube axial and vane axial configurations, different impeller sizes, blade options, drive arrangements, and casing materials, the range can be tailored to different project requirements.</p><p>FanAir India Pvt. Ltd. manufactures axial fans at its Neemrana facility and supplies them to Assam and other locations throughout India. Proper selection based on airflow, static pressure, temperature, fan type, application, and location conditions can help achieve reliable ventilation performance.</p><a href="../contact.php" class="fcx-cta__btn" title="Contact Fan Air India">Contact Us <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section>
